ig menu when foreigners say  that mexicans eat nothing but beans  tacos and chilis  our cuisine definitely stands up in  international comparison  competitive  the chef at donchon knows that  prehispanic cuisine gets little  attention but he thinks it's worthy of  international  junk recognition like pizzas or  hamburgers may taste good  but they're high in carbohydrates and  calories  on the donchon menu you can find  specialties like crocodile in green  pumpkin seed sauce ostrich in plum sauce  venison in pumpkin seed sauce and  pheasant on a bed of rose petals  and you can find grasshoppers like these  there's also a very diverse selection of  desserts  for dessert we have a chocolate amaranth  cake  chocolate is a typical local product  what was that  the chef admits that prehispanic cuisine  is expensive but he says it's worth it  if you really enjoy pre-hispanic cookery  you need money  you do pay a bit more for it  so  creative flavors and unusual textures  characterize this chef's popular cuisine  at the weekend mexico city's more  adventurous diners flock to his  restaurant  that's  here in mexico if people go hungry it's  because they can't be bothered  there's certainly enough good food to go  around  just delicious  for capital 21 this is nancy estrada and  javier cordero  looks delicious  don fortina rojas is not the only chef  experimenting with pre-hispanic cuisine  it's become a trend at high-end  restaurants in mexico city for all of  you intrepid diners out there good luck  now we head to bangladesh where we meet  a brave and bold group of women in the  north of the country who've been  tackling social problems in their  district whether it's alcoholism or  drugs or gambling the women of torch as  their group is called help people in  their communities get back on the right  path etv psychoadliton has the story  this is sudaminishama  unwilling to put up with drug abuse and  related crime spreading through her home  district of arampur she decided 